# A/B: entropy_mul + dist_bias content-discriminated bundle (jxl-encoder-gpu)
# Date: 2026-05-17 UTC
# Commit: see jj log -r @ in jxl-encoder-gpu--entropy-mul-bundle/
# Host: $(hostname) — water-cooled AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB RAM, CUDA
# Bench: cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder-gpu --features 'cuda encoder' \
#        --example auto_entropy_mul_bytes_ab -- --distance {1.0,2.0}
# Images:
#   Screenshots (GB82-SC): terminal.png, imac_g3.png, windows95.png
#   Photos (CLIC2025-1024): 02809272..., 07b9f93f..., 22ea12c9...
#
# Path A (off — production default): LossyEncoder::new(...)
#   .with_auto_evaluate_afv_on_screenshots(false)  // hold AFV constant
#   (default: with_auto_libjxl_entropy_mul_on_photos == false)
#
# Path B (on — experimental opt-in): LossyEncoder::new(...)
#   .with_auto_evaluate_afv_on_screenshots(false)
#   .with_auto_libjxl_entropy_mul_on_photos(true)
#
# Decode: jxl-oxide srgb_linear(Relative) → butteraugli_linear (linear RGB)
#         + fast_ssim2::compute_ssimulacra2 (sRGB u8 — re-linearized)
#
# Audit hypothesis (vardct_gpu_dropped_optimizations_resurrection_2026-05-17.md, item #3+#10):
#   "On photo content the libjxl-faithful values let larger transforms
#    win on smooth regions where they are actually optimal — measured
#    to save bytes on photos at slight bfly cost."
#
# Measured outcome at d=1.0 (entropy_mul_bundle_ab_d1.0_2026-05-17.txt):
#   Screenshots: byte-identical, bfly identical, ssim2 identical. OK.
#   Photos:      bytes +2.5% to +8.5%
#                butteraugli +0.11 to +0.24 (worse)
#                SSIM2 −0.17 to −0.42 (worse)
#   → strictly Pareto-worse on every axis; audit hypothesis REFUTED.
#
# Measured outcome at d=2.0 (entropy_mul_bundle_ab_d2.0_2026-05-17.txt):
#   Screenshots: byte-identical.
#   Photos:      bytes +9% to +13%
#                butteraugli mixed (−0.004 / +0.002 / +1.137 catastrophic on 22ea12c9)
#                SSIM2 −0.10 to −0.28 (one image +0.28)
#   → still strictly worse on bytes; quality degrades catastrophically
#     on detailed content (high d).
#
# Disposition: default to `false`. Dispatch infrastructure kept as
# opt-in for re-validation once `kAvoidEntropyOfTransforms` and the
# X-channel multi-block weight land in GPU cost grids (cross-ref
# dropped log item #4 — multi-week project). The original drop
# rationale stands: removing the GPU-lifted entropy_mul + dist_bias
# counterweights causes over-pick of large transforms regardless of
# content class, because the libjxl heuristics that justify the
# libjxl-faithful values are not present on the GPU encoder.
